            <div xml:id="d584">

                <pb facs="0649" n="537" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg537"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5464: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-23"><hi rendition="#italic">October 23,
                        1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received October 24, 11:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>[From Harris at Omsk:]</p>
                <p>437, October 23, 6 p.m.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Colonel Johnson here in Omsk has just received the following instruction from
                    Colonel Emerson in Harbin: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“As fast as Czechs evacuate back of railway which they are now patrolling
                            you will withdraw all technical inspectors with them.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>The importance of this instruction and the unfortunate impressions it will
                    undoubtedly make on the Russian people is something which the Department may
                    imagine and upon which it is unnecessary for me to comment. Harris.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tenney</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
